# Code owners (#311). A pull request that changes one of these paths asks
# the owners for a review. With "Require review from Code Owners" in the
# branch protection of main, it cannot merge without their approval.
# CONTRIBUTING.md, "Review policy", says why these paths, and the pull
# request template has the security checklist they fill in.
#
# The paths are checked by TestCodeOwners_SecurityPaths
# (internal/codestyle): each one exists, and the template lists the same.

# Authentication, sessions, and second factors
/internal/auth/            @mdastpak
/internal/adminauth/       @mdastpak
/internal/userauth/        @mdastpak
/internal/passkey/         @mdastpak
/internal/passwordhash/    @mdastpak
/internal/otp/             @mdastpak
/internal/totp/            @mdastpak
/internal/identity/        @mdastpak
/internal/signin/          @mdastpak

# Keys, seals, and the audit log
/internal/keys/            @mdastpak
/internal/rowseal/         @mdastpak
/internal/audit/           @mdastpak

# Money: the books, withdrawals, and their confirmation
/internal/ledger/          @mdastpak
/internal/destinations/    @mdastpak
/internal/confirm/         @mdastpak
/internal/verification/    @mdastpak
/internal/crypto/          @mdastpak

# Controls on what users and operators may do
/internal/platform/        @mdastpak
/internal/restrictions/    @mdastpak
/internal/middleware/      @mdastpak

# The schema, the database roles, and the validation of the configuration
/internal/db/migrations/   @mdastpak
/internal/db/roles.go      @mdastpak
/internal/config/validate.go @mdastpak

# What runs in production, and how it is built
/Dockerfile                @mdastpak
/.github/                  @mdastpak
